The file uses this pattern. A product is the physical item. A listing is one place to buy it:

  someIngredient: ingredientFactory('Display Name', {
      products: [{
          brand: 'BrandName',
          variant: 'Variant description',
          size: 16,
          sizeUnit: u.ounce,
          organic: true,
          nutrition: {
              [u.ounce.name]: { servings: 16, servingSize: 1, calories: 100, fat: 0, saturatedFat: 0, transFat: 0, cholesterol: 0, carbs: 0, sodium: 50, sugar: 5, protein: 3, fiber: 2 },
          },
          listings: [{
              store: stores.amazon,
              link: 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DQLSW6FB',
              price: 12.99,
              discount: { subscribeAndSave15: true },
          }],
      }],
  }),

Key rules:
- For Amazon links, strip everything after the ASIN — use https://www.amazon.com/dp/ASIN (e.g. https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DQLSW6FB). Do not include query strings, referral tags, or the product title slug.
- Put store, link, price, and discount on a listing, not on the product. One product can have several listings.
- Store is stores.amazon for Amazon, stores.wholeFoods for Whole Foods, stores.amazonFresh for Amazon Fresh.
- sizeUnit uses u.ounce / u.pound / u.gram / u.cup / u.fluidOunce / u.unit / u.tbsp / u.tsp.
- Nutrition is keyed by the serving size unit (e.g. u.cup.name, u.tbsp.name, u.ounce.name, u.unit.name).
- servingSize is the number of that unit per serving (usually 1); servings is servings per container.
- Include every nutrition field the label shows. Always include fiber — read it from the label if shown; estimate from USDA data if not.
- If the ingredient already exists in the i = { ... } block, add a listing (same SKU, another store) or a product (a different SKU) instead of creating a duplicate ingredient.
- The first product is the default pick. Only add defaultBrand: 'OtherBrand' when a later product should be the pick.
- Add organic: true on the product if it is organic.
- The ingredient key should be camelCase.
- If the same SKU is sold at more than one store, add a listing for each store on that one product. Do not copy the product.
- Subscribe & Save is a boolean tier, not a dollar amount: discount: { subscribeAndSave5: true }, { subscribeAndSave10: true }, or { subscribeAndSave15: true }. Omit discount when the page shows no Subscribe & Save price. The app computes the dollar price from the tier and the current listing price.
- For Whole Foods entries, use the same Amazon product link (https://www.amazon.com/dp/ASIN) — do not fabricate a separate Whole Foods URL. Whole Foods listings do not get a Subscribe & Save discount.

